00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:07.260
And, yes! I already see two things here that&nbsp;
I absolutely love. One, look. A frequent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.200
completely justified criticism of these AI&nbsp;
assistants is that it is sometimes difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.600
to know if they are correct or incorrect.&nbsp;
They learned from people on the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:26.400
and people on the internet are sometimes wrong, so&nbsp;
we should always double check these results. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.760
hold on to your papers, because now&nbsp;
we can do this way easier. How? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:39.240
look! Oh my! It doesn’t just give us an&nbsp;
answer, it also shows what sources it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:45.780
has used, so we can truly double-check these&nbsp;
results. That is the way of the True Scholar.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:54.180
Advantage number two. This is not just a search&nbsp;
query, this is a conversation. So, if we wish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:02.280
we can continue the conversation or make our&nbsp;
question even more specific. And three, if we do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:08.220
it does not just lead us to an already existing&nbsp;
guide. It distills the knowledge from all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:14.400
guides it has seen, and gives us exactly&nbsp;
what we want, and nothing else. No ads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.400
no websites that contain nothing but text&nbsp;
to seduce the search engine to return that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:26.340
one instead of the others. Just what we are&nbsp;
looking for. The answer. I absolutely love it.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:33.480
Fourth, we can also tailor it to our needs. For&nbsp;
instance, if we are a little tired of all these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:40.200
math lessons, we can even ask it to present&nbsp;
